                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "[h1]Update:[/h1]\nThe game is really broken in a few ways, and multiplayer seems to be shutdown, I can't recommend this anymore, sorry...\n\n[h1]TL;DR:[/h1]\nLike Reassembly or Istrolid? You'll like Final Core.\n\n[h1]Positive:[/h1]\n[list]\n[*]Ship building is quick thanks to the various snapping options and shortcuts. All you need to know about your ship is displayed on screen.\n[*]Deep design strategy, there is always a way to defeat a certain design no matter how strong.\n[*]Tons of replayability, you can select one of three playstyles, and there are many choices for special abilities as you level up. There's so many different Sector gimmicks to keep you on your toes.\n[*]Awesome soundtrack I just want to listen to on loop over and over, sound effects are also unique enough to tell apart every weapon.\n[*]Big \"fuck you\" laser weapon.\n[*]Able to quickly switch from cruising to strafing, in*action settings can change how your ship behaves.\n[*]HUD displays part integrity, which is useful to avoid part destruction.\n[*]Most weapons can fire in 360 degrees, and all parts can be rotated to whatever direction you want.\n[*]Aimbot can be enabled so you can focus on piloting your ship, I find this especially helpful against enemies that fill the screen with bullets.\n[/list]\n\n[h1]Negative:[/h1]\n[list]\n[*]Final Core is very repetitive, but that's just the nature of every game isn't it? (Rhetorical, don't answer.)\n[*]There is a grind to be able to build the biggest baddest ships, it will take a while before you can fight the toughest champions.\n[*]Some Sectors are completely unfair.\n[*]You can only use one color, and choosing the same color as an enemy team becomes confusing sometimes.\n[/list]\n\n[h1]Conclusion:[/h1]\n(In my opinion) Final Core is a very strong competitor in the fleet-building genre, I'm surprised it's made by one person. I can't wait to see what's in store for the future.",
